# Safety net. vigil already pushes on every write (write_and_commit reports an
# error to the client when the push fails). This cron job only covers the
# window where a push failed at write time — say GitHub was briefly
# unreachable — and the commit has been sitting locally ever since.
#
# Install into the vigil user's crontab (crontab -u vigil -e), or as a file at
# /etc/cron.d/vigil-push-safety-net (then with a user field:
# "*/15 * * * * vigil cd ...").
#
# Pushes only when commits are actually pending, takes a lock against a
# concurrent write_and_commit, and sends errors to syslog rather than nowhere.

*/15 * * * * cd /var/lib/vigil/vault && \
  git rev-list --count github/main..main | grep -qv '^0$' && \
  flock -n /tmp/vigil-push.lock git push github main 2>&1 | logger -t vigil-push
